WEBVTT

00:00:00.290 --> 00:00:03.700
You ask your agent to sort a list, newest first.

00:00:04.370 --> 00:00:05.880
Dunn nods at anything.

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:09.270
The agent clicks where the menu was yesterday.

00:00:10.090 --> 00:00:11.480
It says done.

00:00:11.910 --> 00:00:12.840
Dunn nods.

00:00:13.090 --> 00:00:15.270
The list hasn’t moved.

00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:23.490
Desktop Tasks names the finish line before the first click.

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:30.370
It reads the screen two ways, picture and labelled controls, and acts when they agree.

00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:33.510
It looks again.

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:37.670
The newest task is on top, and the receipt says how it knows.

00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:43.810
Success with no visible change is ambiguous.

00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:47.950
It looks twice at most, then stops and tells you.

00:00:48.170 --> 00:00:51.060
It needs a computer-use tool and your permission.

00:00:51.490 --> 00:00:54.710
Its tests ran on a pretend desktop.

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:05.890
Desktop Tasks.

00:01:06.140 --> 00:01:07.370
Finish the task.

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:09.410
Check the screen that proves it.
